{"author":{"id":"29588b87a98184856c6eb9104921c34cca98a9cb029a2ee86cc10622d693ba86"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1794875231,"nonce":"oTWQ7ygjgau4JnY3bPJXngjwXO4=","target":"ec4693d9e744f5d9fd8f2f3b58db4aaade97c87e9755f084f36833894add73ec","message":"We are building a shared menu model (menubar, menu, menuitem with checkbox and radio variants, separator, tree/treeitem, toolbar, dialog) on top of Blinc, and we want it to be usable with a screen reader.\n\nWhat we found in the source (checked against the commit we build on, cf925af, and against current main; the files named below are identical in both):\n\n- blinc_layout already builds a platform-independent semantic tree: RenderTree::accessibility_nodes() (crates/blinc_layout/src/renderer/accessibility.rs:10) returns nodes with role, label, value, disabled, selected, checked, expanded and focused (crates/blinc_layout/src/accessibility.rs:60-76). Labels come from aria-label / aria-labelledby, state from aria-checked / aria-expanded / aria-selected / aria-disabled.\n- The only consumer is the iOS backend (crates/blinc_app/src/ios/accessibility.rs, with the Swift UIAccessibilityElement side in extensions/blinc_platform_ios/swift/BlincAccessibility.swift). We found no consumer in extensions/blinc_platform_desktop, and no dependency on AccessKit or a similar crate in any Cargo.toml. Android only marks its IME view as not important for accessibility (extensions/blinc_platform_android/templates/BlincIme.kt:69), and the web book lists ARIA/screen reader support as pending (docs/book/src/web/overview.md:104). So on the desktop, nothing reaches assistive technology.\n- The role set is small: AccessibilityRole has Text, Heading, Button, Link, TextField, Checkbox, Switch, Radio, Slider, Tab, MenuItem, Image (crates/blinc_layout/src/accessibility.rs:9-22). role=\"menuitem\", \"menuitemcheckbox\" and \"menuitemradio\" all map to MenuItem (crates/blinc_layout/src/renderer/accessibility.rs:206). We found no role for menubar, menu, separator, tree, treeitem, toolbar or dialog (the mapping is at renderer/accessibility.rs:190-235).\n\nKeyboard operation works, so the menus can be driven, but nothing is announced on the desktop.\n\nRequest: desktop accessibility support, for example through AccessKit (https://github.com/AccessKit/accesskit), consuming the existing semantic tree, with\n- the missing roles (menubar, menu, separator, tree, treeitem, toolbar, dialog) and a way to tell the checkbox/radio menu item variants apart,\n- the names and states that already exist (expanded, checked, selected, disabled) delivered to the platform,\n- focus notifications, so a screen reader follows the focused item.\n\nIf it helps, a small prototype or a short guide for wiring a widget to the accessibility tree would already be a good start. We are happy to test with Orca on Linux and NVDA on Windows and to contribute test cases. We are also willing to help with a pull request. There is no hurry on our side.","files":null}]}